WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.840
Our cells have two copies of all our genetic&nbsp;
information meaning we have two copies of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:15.920
each gene in every cell of our body. Cancer can&nbsp;
develop when cells acquire mutations over time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.920
Both copies of a gene need to be&nbsp;
mutated for cancer to develop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.160
Gene mutations can be either inherited&nbsp;
or acquired. Inherited mutations are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.640
called germline mutations and acquired&nbsp;
mutations are called somatic mutations.&nbsp;

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:37.120
Somatic mutations or acquired mutations happen&nbsp;
when genes mutate over a person's lifetime and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:44.000
are present in the tumor. They are not inherited&nbsp;
or passed down to children. Somatic mutations may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:51.920
be caused by environmental factors, habits, diet,&nbsp;
or by chance. Most cancers are caused by somatic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:58.560
mutations. Currently we cannot determine the exact&nbsp;
cause of somatic mutations in individual patients.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.480
Inherited mutations or germline mutations are&nbsp;
typically passed down from one of your parents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:11.840
Approximately five to ten percent of&nbsp;
cancers are due to inherited gene mutations.

